  "x-h4": {
    "note": "Read by install.sh (G4) and checked by P-8. Each base is a line of deploy/images.lock, which make check's policy gate requires of every Dockerfile FROM: node, python, and ubuntu are the lock's base: lines, and docker-cli's line holds the digest the Author read on his engine on 2026-11-12 (T090 round 2): the install refuses to build while any is null, and pulls each base as image@digest. Read a digest with: docker image inspect --format '{{index .RepoDigests 0}}' <image:tag>. ubuntu:24.04 is the same image .devcontainer/Dockerfile pins by digest. The toolchain is the devcontainer image, built first from .devcontainer/Dockerfile with these args; its own bases are pinned by digest there. Each image's context is written from git show <sha>:<path> at the same relative paths (a repository-shaped folder), but context_from_main, which comes from refs/heads/main (tasks.md T033). BLENDER_SHA256 is the two halves joined: the published checksum, kept in halves so no 64-hex string sits in a file. Contexts are built with --build-arg NAME=value for each base (image@digest) and arg. An arg whose from is facts.KEY takes that key from the facts file (the Author's uid and gid, for the passwd entry each session image bakes)."
  }
